# Files irrelevant to BOTH deployables — kept out of the `railway up` upload
# snapshot (the Railway CLI honors .ignore). Only genuine build artifacts, the
# monorepo mirror, long-form docs, and datasets.
#
# WARNING: the RUNNER service (runner/Dockerfile does `COPY . .`) needs the
# FULL repo at runtime — run.py, scripts/, setup.py, hostadmin/, src/,
# Cargo.*, initial_algorithms/ — because it runs whole fleets per contributor.
# Do NOT re-add those here or `railway up` for the runner ships a broken image.
# The server image only COPYs server/ + initial_algorithms/ + built dist, so
# the extra files in the upload are harmless (and unused) for it.
docs/
tig-monorepo/
target/
datasets/
# Local state and generated agent output are not image inputs. Most are also
# covered by .gitignore, but listing them here keeps Railway snapshots small
# even if uploader ignore precedence changes.
worktrees/
local/
reports/
prompts_log/
feedback/
*.db
*.db-journal
swarm.admin*.json
